WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.169 --> 00:00:02.904
- I love when things melt in my mouth.

00:00:02.904 --> 00:00:05.987
(upbeat jazzy music)

00:00:11.688 --> 00:00:14.149
- We're here today at
Sul &amp; Beans in Koreatown.

00:00:14.149 --> 00:00:17.482
- And we're gonna try Korean shaved ice.

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.950
- I've never tried
Korean shaved ice before.

00:00:26.950 --> 00:00:29.231
I've had the spicier side of Korean food,

00:00:29.231 --> 00:00:30.403
but not the sweet side.

00:00:30.403 --> 00:00:31.820
- I've never had shaved ice.

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.034
I've had a snow cone.

00:00:33.034 --> 00:00:33.867
I really don't know what to expect.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:34.700
- Yeah.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.541
- I don't know what it is.

00:00:35.541 --> 00:00:36.682
- I used to have that when I was little

00:00:36.682 --> 00:00:37.637
when I lived in Korea.

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:40.370
- We are ready to eat
some damn shaved ice.

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:43.287
(funky rock music)

00:00:45.466 --> 00:00:46.746
- This is not at all what I expected.

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:47.579
- Me either.

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:48.666
This is like a delicacy.

00:00:48.666 --> 00:00:49.751
- This is condensed milk.

00:00:49.751 --> 00:00:51.346
You're supposed to spread it on top of it.

00:00:51.346 --> 00:00:53.506
- This is the most magical
thing I've ever seen.

00:00:53.506 --> 00:00:54.720
- It looks like snow.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:56.700
- It reminds me of a cheesecake almost.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:58.367
- Mmm. It's so good.

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:00.662
(laughing)

00:01:00.662 --> 00:01:01.495
- What is this?

00:01:01.495 --> 00:01:02.986
- You know that expression,

00:01:02.986 --> 00:01:04.569
oh, it's just melting in my mouth.

00:01:04.569 --> 00:01:05.402
- This is just really good.

00:01:05.402 --> 00:01:07.335
I'm trying to compare it to something.

00:01:07.335 --> 00:01:08.310
I don't think I can.

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:10.635
- This is so [Bleep] good.

00:01:10.635 --> 00:01:13.718
(funky upbeat music)

00:01:16.271 --> 00:01:17.470
- Okay, this is beautiful.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:20.470
- It reminds me of an Asian temple.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:21.763
- This is a masterpiece.

00:01:21.763 --> 00:01:23.054
I'm scared to [Bleep] it up.

00:01:23.054 --> 00:01:24.474
- You know it's a good dessert

00:01:24.474 --> 00:01:27.023
when you have to take photos of it.

00:01:27.023 --> 00:01:28.499
- This is much more earthy,

00:01:28.499 --> 00:01:30.180
so I think red beans

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.092
are kind of a delicacy dessert in Asia.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:33.466
- I just want to eat all the beans.

00:01:33.466 --> 00:01:36.793
- I've never had ice that's
this finely shaved before.

00:01:36.793 --> 00:01:37.626
- Yeah.

00:01:37.626 --> 00:01:38.470
- It's amazing.

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:39.819
- It's very smooth.

00:01:39.819 --> 00:01:42.442
- Very healthy tasting, it's interesting.

00:01:42.442 --> 00:01:44.109
- It's bomb dot com.

00:01:48.153 --> 00:01:49.625
- [Both] Oh.

00:01:49.625 --> 00:01:52.195
I really know already that
I'm going to love this.

00:01:52.195 --> 00:01:53.289
- It's so crafty.

00:01:53.289 --> 00:01:54.851
I feel kinda guilty about ...

00:01:54.851 --> 00:01:55.684
- Messing it up.

00:01:55.684 --> 00:01:56.652
- I don't wanna touch it,

00:01:56.652 --> 00:01:58.109
but I also know when I touch it

00:01:58.109 --> 00:02:02.174
it will be the most
magical moment of my life.

00:02:02.174 --> 00:02:05.657
- This tastes like an American
version of Korean shaved ice.

00:02:05.657 --> 00:02:06.829
- It's so creamy.

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:08.414
- I think there's little bits

00:02:08.414 --> 00:02:09.247
of cream cheese in there, too.

00:02:09.247 --> 00:02:10.190
- It's not cheesecake.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.249
- The cheesecake is
made with cream cheese.

00:02:13.249 --> 00:02:14.082
(laughing)

00:02:14.082 --> 00:02:16.198
- Cheesecake bites inside of the ice.

00:02:16.198 --> 00:02:19.590
You keep digging and you just
keep on bringing up gold.

00:02:19.590 --> 00:02:21.681
- The ice is, it's so fine.

00:02:21.681 --> 00:02:23.095
It's like biting into a cold cloud.

00:02:23.095 --> 00:02:24.047
- It feels like snow, yeah.

00:02:24.047 --> 00:02:27.964
- It's so much softer
than American shaved ice.

00:02:36.734 --> 00:02:38.140
- Oh, we have a little toast.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.430
- Trying to make me fat.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:40.263
- I'm okay with it.

00:02:40.263 --> 00:02:42.152
- This looks much like cheese strudel

00:02:42.152 --> 00:02:43.848
and I love cheese strudel.

00:02:43.848 --> 00:02:44.722
- This is pretty.

00:02:44.722 --> 00:02:48.297
It's like something out of Zelda.

00:02:48.297 --> 00:02:49.844
- Yes, oh my God.

00:02:49.844 --> 00:02:51.319
- I love green tea, it's so good.

00:02:51.319 --> 00:02:53.606
- This is just really satisfying.

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:56.079
- This is like the one that you wanna eat

00:02:56.079 --> 00:02:59.004
after Korean barbecue
because it wakes your ass up.

00:02:59.004 --> 00:03:00.733
- Yeah, it tastes a lot
like the green tea mochis.

00:03:00.733 --> 00:03:02.040
- Oh my god, I can't wait.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:02.880
I'm doing this now.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:03.713
- Wait, how do you do this?

00:03:03.713 --> 00:03:05.846
- Alright, cheers.

00:03:05.846 --> 00:03:07.861
- It tastes like a sweet grilled cheese.

00:03:07.861 --> 00:03:09.088
- I thought it was gonna
taste more like pizza.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.828
It's sugary, it's like
honey grilled cheese.

00:03:11.828 --> 00:03:13.406
- That is so good.

00:03:13.406 --> 00:03:15.943
- It's like a sweet
and savory honey toast.

00:03:15.943 --> 00:03:19.546
And this rice cake has
a cheesy consistency.

00:03:19.546 --> 00:03:21.545
- On the bottom it's slightly toasted,

00:03:21.545 --> 00:03:23.391
so it's got a little bit of resistance.

00:03:23.391 --> 00:03:24.347
I wanna move in here.

00:03:24.347 --> 00:03:26.328
(light music)

00:03:26.328 --> 00:03:27.936
- Child, I've never had it before,

00:03:27.936 --> 00:03:28.783
but I will have it again.

00:03:28.783 --> 00:03:30.345
- A lot of different textures.

00:03:30.345 --> 00:03:31.178
- Yeah.

00:03:31.178 --> 00:03:32.058
- A lot of different flavors

00:03:32.058 --> 00:03:33.199
that really played off well.

00:03:33.199 --> 00:03:34.256
And it just looked beautiful.

00:03:34.256 --> 00:03:36.409
- This place actually
brought back all my memories.

00:03:36.409 --> 00:03:37.609
It was so good.

00:03:37.609 --> 00:03:40.394
- I didn't know shaved ice
could be so spectacular.

00:03:40.394 --> 00:03:43.289
- Every now and then, you need
a nice cool refreshing treat.

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:45.171
And I feel like this
would be like perfect.

00:03:45.171 --> 00:03:47.451
- I really think it's
the perfect date food.

00:03:47.451 --> 00:03:48.491
There's enough for everyone.

00:03:48.491 --> 00:03:49.326
- Yeah.

00:03:49.326 --> 00:03:50.233
- And it's beautiful to look at

00:03:50.233 --> 00:03:51.102
and it's very romantic.

00:03:51.102 --> 00:03:52.956
- There's this place
nextdoor called SomiSomi.

00:03:52.956 --> 00:03:55.642
They sell this traditional
Korean ice cream.

00:03:55.642 --> 00:03:56.717
- It's a fishy.

00:03:56.717 --> 00:03:58.651
It has good color in it.

